      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(cli): add --file option to image generate command",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`openclaw infer image generate` cannot accept input/reference images via `--file`, making it impossible to use CLI workflows for image-conditioned generation. The sibling `image edit` command already supports `--file`, and the shared `runImageGenerate` helper already handles `inputImages` — the only gap is the CLI option registration and docs.\n\nCloses #91734\n\n## Fix\n\n- Added `--file <path>` as an optional flag to `image generate` CLI registration\n- Updated `docs/cli/infer.md` with example\n- Added forwarding test\n\n## Evidence\n\n### CLI proof — --file flag accepted\n\n```text\n$ openclaw infer image generate --help\n  ... --output --json --file\n\n$ openclaw infer image generate --file /tmp/test.png --prompt \"test\" --json\n  # CLI accepts --file flag (no \"unknown option\" error)\n```\n\n### Test suite\n\n```\nnpx vitest run src/cli/capability-cli.test.ts\n  Test Files 1 passed  Tests 98 passed\n```\n\n### Formatting\n\n```\npnpm exec oxfmt --check ...  (pass)\ngit diff --check  (clean)\n```\n\n## Change Type\n\n- [x] Feature\n\n## Scope\n\n- [x] CLI (image generate)\n\n## Security Impact\n\n- New permissions? No\n- Secrets handling changed? No\n- New network calls? No",
        "branch": "fix/91734-image-generate-file-option",
        "head_sha": "6dae1c23e41138a39d4552a69bd7e563d26b6cc6",
